From 5d344efea99a9339dd51c78c5ee677e66f217e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:58:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] app-info: Identify Luma applications

Applications Luma installs from package files run in the
luma_application.process SELinux domain under a category pair allocated
to them, in their own app-luma-NAME-PID.scope. Name them through Luma's
resolver (org.projectluma.AppPermissions1.Identify, the rules Mutter 0041
uses) and treat them as sandboxed: permissions are stored under their ID
and files they are given go through the document portal. One that cannot
be named is refused instead of being treated as the host.
---
